{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_12-22-18-hashicorp_raft-real-run && python3 -c \\\"\nimport json;s=json.load(open('submission.schema.json'));print(json.dumps(s['\\\\\"'$defs'\"']['KnowledgeUse'],indent=1));print(json.dumps(s['\\\\\"'$defs'\"']['SourceAnchor'],indent=1)[:300])\\\"\"","aggregated_output":"{\n \"additionalProperties\": false,\n \"properties\": {\n  \"entry_id\": {\n   \"title\": \"Entry Id\",\n   \"type\": \"string\"\n  },\n  \"revision\": {\n   \"minimum\": 1,\n   \"title\": \"Revision\",\n   \"type\": \"integer\"\n  },\n  \"assertion\": {\n   \"default\": \"\",\n   \"title\": \"Assertion\",\n   \"type\": \"string\"\n  }\n },\n \"required\": [\n  \"entry_id\",\n  \"revision\"\n ],\n \"title\": \"KnowledgeUse\",\n \"type\": \"object\"\n}\n{\n \"additionalProperties\": false,\n \"properties\": {\n  \"material_id\": {\n   \"title\": \"Material Id\",\n   \"type\": \"string\"\n  },\n  \"symbol\": {\n   \"title\": \"Symbol\",\n   \"type\": \"string\"\n  },\n  \"start_line\": {\n   \"minimum\": 1,\n   \"title\": \"Start Line\",\n   \"type\": \"integer\"\n  },\n  \"end_line\": {\n   \"minimum\": \n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_12-22-18-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nst=json.load(open('../state.json'))\nrec=[i for i in st['interpretations'] if i.get('id')=='8e037ca743394e1a8a518b9745b8fe53-interpretation-0'][0]\n\ninterp={\n \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"3b823834c8cb46da98e77d8e988bf5d9-question-0\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":list(dict.fromkeys(rec['source_ids']+[\\\"elect_vote_collection\\\",\\\"prevote_vote_collection\\\",\\\"vote_grant_side\\\"])),\n \\\"executions\\\":rec['executions'],\n \\\"conclusion\\\":rec['conclusion'],\n \\\"defect_claim\\\":rec['defect_claim'],\n \\\"rationale\\\":rec['rationale']+\\\" \\\"\n   \\\"The same file shows the omission is not a considered relaxation of voter eligibility: electSelf and preElectSelf build the very same voter-sized threshold, and both iterate the leader's latest configuration asking only servers whose Suffrage is Voter, so a candidate neither solicits nor counts a non-voter's grant even though nothing on the granting side stops a non-voter from granting a vote if it were asked. Only the verify path asks every replication peer. That contrast is recorded as its own Behaviour so the finding is not reused without it, and it turns the question's answer from 'the success signal is weaker than its documentation' into 'the success signal contradicts the eligibility rule the same decisions use everywhere else'.\\\",\n \\\"knowledge\\\":[{\\\"entry_id\\\":rec and \\\"@elect_voter_only_solicitation\\\", \\\"revision\\\":1,\n   \\\"assertion\\\":\\\"Election vote solicitation asks only servers whose Suffrage is Voter, so the verify path's inclusion of non-voters is an omission rather than the intended eligibility rule.\\\"}],\n \\\"answers\\\":rec['answers'],\n \\\"counterevidence\\\":rec['counterevidence'],\n \\\"limitations\\\":rec['limitations']}\n\nknowledge={\n \\\"ref\\\":\\\"@elect_voter_only_solicitation\\\",\n \\\"kind\\\":\\\"behavior\\\",\n \\\"statement\\\":\\\"Election vote solicitation is restricted to voters, unlike the verify path in the same file. electSelf and preElectSelf both iterate configurations.latest.Servers and act only when server.Suffrage == Voter: the local server records a vote for itself and every other server is asked with a RequestVote or RequestPreVote RPC, while non-voters are skipped altogether, so no non-voter grant is ever counted toward the voter-sized quorum they compare against. The grant side is not what keeps non-voters out: requestVote rejects a candidate that holds no vote and a candidate that is not in the configuration, but it imposes no suffrage requirement on the server granting, and it persists and grants a vote whenever the candidate's log is at least as up to date, so a non-voter would grant if it were asked. verifyLeader is the path that does ask every entry of leaderState.replState, which includes non-voters.\\\",\n \\\"conditions\\\":\\\"A server whose latest configuration contains non-voting members, with pre-vote either enabled (preElectSelf) or disabled (electSelf directly); the solicitation loops read configurations.latest on the candidate's own main thread.\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"elect_vote_collection\\\",\\\"prevote_vote_collection\\\",\\\"vote_grant_side\\\",\\\"verify_leader\\\",\\\"follower_vote_grant\\\"]}\n\nd={\\\"rationale\\\":(\\\"Recorded the differential that decides how the VerifyLeader finding should be read: the election path solicits votes only from servers whose Suffrage is Voter (electSelf and preElectSelf), while verifyLeader asks every replication peer including non-voters, and the granting side would have granted a non-voter's vote if it had been asked. This adds that Behaviour and re-states the verify question's account with the contrast, without changing the question's evidence or its conditional consequence.\\\"),\n \\\"sources\\\":[\n  {\\\"id\\\":\\\"elect_vote_collection\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"raft.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":1999,\\\"end_line\\\":2064,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n  {\\\"id\\\":\\\"prevote_vote_collection\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"raft.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":2073,\\\"end_line\\\":2150,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n  {\\\"id\\\":\\\"vote_grant_side\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"raft.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":1660,\\\"end_line\\\":1700,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"}],\n \\\"knowledge\\\":[knowledge],\n \\\"interpretations\\\":[interp]}\njson.dump(d,open('update.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False); open('update.json','a').write('\\\\n')\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_12-22-18-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -3\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
